# Merge policy for upstream (Handy) syncs — see Upstream/UPSTREAM.md.
#
# `merge=ours` keeps Grain's version whenever a file conflicts during an
# upstream merge. It requires the driver to be defined once per clone:
#     git config merge.ours.driver true
# Without that config the attribute is silently ignored and a normal
# merge happens instead (safe fallback).
#
# Only list files Grain fully owns — where upstream's version is never
# wanted. Shared code (src-tauri/src/) must NOT be listed: we want upstream
# fixes there, and real conflicts should surface. `src/` used to be in that
# category and no longer is — see the frontend freeze below.

# Grain-owned docs and repo meta
README.md          merge=ours
AGENTS.md          merge=ours
CLAUDE.md          merge=ours
CRUSH.md           merge=ours
BUILD.md           merge=ours
CONTRIBUTING.md    merge=ours
CONTRIBUTING_TRANSLATIONS.md merge=ours
docs/**            merge=ours
website/**         merge=ours
Upstream/**        merge=ours

# Grain-owned CI (upstream workflows do not apply to this repo)
.github/workflows/** merge=ours

# [GRAIN] Frontend freeze — see docs/UI 2.0/PLAN.md.
# The UI is being rewritten wholesale, so upstream's React tree is no longer a
# base we build on. Measured before deciding: of upstream's last 22 commits, 17
# touched the backend and 4 touched the frontend outside i18n — two of those for
# features Grain deleted, two carrying *backend* knowledge (host accelerators,
# locale resolution) that belongs in Rust, where we still merge everything.
# merge=ours only wins conflicts, so the freeze is enforced by
# Upstream/frontend_freeze.py, not by this line alone.
src/** merge=ours

# App identity: com.grain.app, no auto-updater. Review upstream conf
# changes manually (git log upstream/main -- src-tauri/tauri.conf.json).
src-tauri/tauri.conf.json         merge=ours
src-tauri/tauri.windows.conf.json merge=ours

# Lockfiles: keep ours during the merge, then REGENERATE
# (bun install / cargo update -p <crate> as needed) before committing.
bun.lock           merge=ours
Cargo.lock         merge=ours
src-tauri/Cargo.lock merge=ours

# Shared rerere resolutions (Upstream/rerere_cache.py): pre/postimages must
# stay byte-exact or rerere's conflict hashes stop matching — never convert
# line endings.
Upstream/rr-cache/** -text

# Font binaries must never be line-ending converted (would corrupt the file).
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff2 binary

# [GRAIN] Phase 5A signed seed catalogue: the minisign signature is computed
# over the EXACT bytes of each .json, so line-ending conversion on checkout
# would break verification cross-platform. Keep the whole seed dir byte-exact.
crates/grain-core/seed/** -text

# [GRAIN] Phase 5B signed store fixtures — verified over exact bytes; never
# line-ending convert or the committed signatures stop matching.
src-tauri/tests/fixtures/store/** -text
